---
// Bio text matches the current live site (Webflow homepage).
---

<section class="profile" id="about" aria-labelledby="profile-title">
  <div>
    <span class="label">(02) Profile</span>
    <h2 class="display" id="profile-title">
      Serious about music.<br />
      <em>Relentless</em> in the pursuit of meaning.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="copy">
    <p class="lead">
      Jon works across musical genres as a composer, arranger and conductor, from his base in
      Scotland.
    </p>
    <div class="columns">
      <p>
        His professional portfolio over the last 10 years encompasses artistic directorships;
        conducting new music, as well as standard orchestral repertoire and opera;
        composing/arranging for orchestras, singer-songwriters and other artists; and executive
        production for recording projects.
      </p>
      <p>
        He co-founded the Octandre Ensemble with the composer Christian Mason in 2011. He has
        conducted and led the Ensemble in festival appearances in London and at the Huddersfield
        Contemporary Music Festival, leading to appearances on BBC Radio 3, and CD releases on
        Another Timbre and SN Variations. He was founding Co-Artistic Director of Glasgow's Nevis
        Ensemble until 2022, conducting over 200 performances in settings ranging from schools and
        prisons to museums, art galleries and concert halls, as well as on top of Ben Nevis and on
        the remote isles of St Kilda. Since 2023, he conducts the Film Composers Lab at the Royal
        Scottish National Orchestra (RSNO).
      </p>
      <p>
        Jon has a long-term and deep-rooted interest in musical value and meaning. He has published
        music analytic work, as well as collaborations in the social psychology of music, music
        education and embodied music cognition. Jon teaches at the Royal Conservatoire of Scotland.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <blockquote>
        “Denyer’s hour-long masterpiece … had a gripping flow that was sometimes thunderously
        aggressive, … sometimes beguiling and often disturbing.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption class="label">
        Richard Morrison, The Times —
        <a href="/projects/the-fish-that-became-the-sun-world-premiere">
          The Fish that Became the Sun
        </a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .profile {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 9vw;
    margin-top: 130px;
    padding: var(--section-space) var(--gutter) 130px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: clamp(55px, 7vw, 100px);
  }

  h2 em {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .copy {
    padding-top: 38px;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 580px;
    margin: 0 0 48px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 30px;
  }

  .columns p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  figure {
    margin: 70px 0 0;
    padding: 28px 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 27px;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  figcaption a {
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .profile {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
    }

    .copy {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .profile {
      margin-top: 85px;
      padding-bottom: var(--section-space);
    }

    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
